# S3 Presigned URLs (Upload)

## Security

- **Allowed types:** Whitelist MIME types and extensions; enforce max size per type; reject unknown types
- **Expiration:** Short (5–15 min) for upload URLs
- **Key generation:** Server-generated key (e.g. `uploads/{userId}/{uuid}/{filename}`); sanitize client filename; no path traversal
- **Validation:** After upload, validate content-type (e.g. with file-type) and size server-side; do not trust client headers only
- **Bucket:** Private; access only via presigned URL or Lambda with IAM

## Implementation

- **Client:** `@aws-sdk/client-s3`, `@aws-sdk/s3-request-presigner`; `PutObjectCommand` with Key, ContentType, ContentLength (optional but recommended); sign with `getSignedUrl(client, command, { expiresIn })`
- **Handler:** Validate user/auth; check requested ContentType and size against allowlist; generate key; return presigned URL and key to client
- **Post-upload:** Client notifies API (key, optional hash); API validates object in S3 (headObject, content-type/size) and then processes

## Conventions

- Always allowlist types and size; short expiry; server-generated keys; post-upload validation

## Anti-Patterns

- Client-supplied key without sanitization; no MIME/size validation; long expiry; public bucket

